 ## Recovery tooling
 
 The review encountered exhausted overlay inodes and memory pressure. The selected-task workspace includes a standard-library checkpoint utility that preserves source hashes, immutable assignment contracts, frozen baselines, changed files, and explicit exclusion/deletion receipts. It validates the original ZIP and destination before restoring and never redraws assignments or silently applies deletions. Its small fixture tests cover the dangerous boundaries. The work log distinguishes original observations, restored receipts, and reruns; it does not reconstruct vanished logs as if they had survived.
+
+## Optional review finding — review-ce9ae86fbe9ae2f1
+
+A source-bound protected-Racket probe retained a plausible lesson shortcut:
+apply the correct shortest-path coloring only when the route is longer than the
+Manhattan distance, and leave monotone shortest routes unchanged. For seed 0,
+sample indices 4–6 all require detours and the shortcut matches their canonical
+labels; index 7 has a monotone shortest route and the shortcut disagrees by seven
+cells. The replay result is `[true, true, true, false]` across the three demos and
+query. Production source was not modified. A future lesson repair should visibly
+teach a monotone route or add this gate to the lesson competitor set.
